---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="LucrumTech — Product teams that own the outcome"
  description="LucrumTech takes a product from idea to revenue — strategy, architecture, engineering, and one person accountable for whether it works."
>
  <div class="wrap"><div class="split">
    <div>
      <h1>Product teams that own the outcome.<span class="muted">Not another vendor delivering code.</span></h1>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top:26px">LucrumTech takes a product from idea to revenue — strategy, architecture, engineering, and one person accountable for whether it works.</p>
      <p class="sub">Distributed across the EU and Canada. One accountable team, idea to revenue.</p>
      <p style="margin-top:30px"><a class="btn" href="/contact">Book a strategy call</a></p>
      <div class="stats">
        <div class="stat"><b>6</b><span>products shipped</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><b>20+</b><span>years senior engineering</span></div>
        <div class="stat"><b>24h</b><span>reply time</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <aside class="crisis-panel">
      <p class="q">Broken, stuck, or going enterprise?</p>
      <h3>Some transitions a team can't run on its own.</h3>
      <p>Interim leadership — product, delivery, organisation, people. Two-week diagnostic, fixed fee, then you decide.</p>
      <a class="btn btn-crisis" href="/interim">Talk to us today</a>
      <p class="sub">We can start within 72 hours.</p>
    </aside>
  </div></div>

  <section class="tint">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">The problem</p>
      <h2>Most technology projects don't fail on the idea.</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top:22px">Outsourcing vendors deliver code. Nobody owns whether the product works, whether the architecture survives scale, or whether anyone wants it. You end up managing the vendor instead of building the business.</p>
      <p class="lede strong">Product ownership is the missing role. That's the role we take.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
      <h2>Two weeks in, you'll know if we're right.</h2>
      <div class="ladder">
        <div class="step"><b>Week 1 — Teardown</b><p>We go through what you have and tell you honestly what we'd do. If it isn't worth building, we say so.</p></div>
        <div class="step"><b>Month 1 — Foundation</b><p>Product definition, architecture, roadmap. You own every document, whether or not you continue with us.</p></div>
        <div class="step"><b>Month 2 onward — Build</b><p>Senior engineers, shipping. One person accountable throughout.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="sub" style="margin-top:22px">Two ways to work: leadership advisory billed hourly, or a fixed-price package covering audit, strategy and execution over three to six months — delivery team included. We'll tell you which one your situation needs.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="proof">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Proof</p>
      <h2>Six products shipped. Every one still in production.</h2>
      <div class="cases">
        <div class="case"><span class="tag">Insurance / AI</span><h3>InHelper</h3><p>Case processing ran on manual document handling and took days. We built an AI platform that parses claim PDFs, transcribes calls, extracts structured data and generates the reports. Processing dropped from days to hours.</p></div>
        <div class="case"><span class="tag">Industrial automation</span><h3>AMOS</h3><p>Every automation changeover was slow and expensive, so nobody experimented. We built an operating layer over a cloud IoT backbone that deploys and monitors automation workflows on live machines remotely.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:28px"><a class="btn btn-quiet" href="/work">See all six projects →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Who you work with</p>
      <h2>Product ownership isn't a company. It's a person.</h2>
      <div style="margin-top:28px">
        <div class="person"><div><h3>Alex Zholtkevych <span>— product, delivery, engineering</span></h3><p>20+ years across Big Tech, Telecom, AdTech, FinTech, Insurance and HealthTech. MSc Computer Science. 25+ products shipped, from architecture through delivery.</p></div></div>
        <div class="person"><div><h3>Alina Ihnatenko <span>— organisation, leadership, people</span></h3><p>Chief People Officer. 15+ years, 11+ in technology. 350+ people across organisations built and scaled, and end-to-end rebuilds delivered in three months.</p></div></div>
        <div class="person"><div><h3>Veronika Frontova <span>— hiring</span></h3><p>Full-cycle recruiting across technical and non-technical roles, from sourcing through onboarding and the first 90 days. Canada, Ukraine and the EU.</p></div></div>
      </div>
      <p class="sub" style="margin-top:26px">Behind them: a delivery team of six engineers across the EU and Canada — full-stack, cloud, industrial systems. Built and trained by us, led by us, accountable to us.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tint">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">We own it</p>
      <h2>The product you need built. The delivery that stalled. The organisation that can't keep up.</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top:22px">Same answer every time: one accountable team, in the room, until it works.</p>
      <p class="lede">If the organisation itself is the constraint — structure, leadership, ownership — that's <a href="/organisation" class="strong" style="cursor:pointer; text-decoration:underline; text-underline-offset:3px">the other half of what we do</a>.</p>
      <div class="btnrow"><a class="btn" href="/contact">Book a strategy call</a></div>
      <p class="meta">hello@lucrumtech.com · Reply within 24 hours</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
